{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "d4e8b3a1-6f2c-4b9e-8a71-2c5f9e0d1b47",
    "name": "Lab 9 - StockFlow in Docker",
    "description": "Lab 9 - StockFlow running in Docker.\n\nPoint baseUrl at the containerized stack (http://localhost:8080 after `docker compose up`) and run TOP TO BOTTOM in the Collection Runner. Request 0 hits /actuator/health without a token - that is the same question the compose healthcheck asks.\n\nThe Setup folder registers clerk bob, logs in admin and bob, and builds the fixture (category, supplier, a product with a unique SKU per run). The Ledger folder is the heart of the domain: IN 250, OUT 30, an OUT that cannot be honoured (409), and the product's running balance read straight off the history. The Authorization folder proves the CLERK/ADMIN split and that every refused delete is a 409, never a 500.\n\nRe-running is safe: registration and fixture creation accept 409, the SKU carries a timestamp, and nothing is deleted.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
